    {"id": "v05-kopun", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 5, "badge": "OLD DUBROVNIK", "name": "Kopun", "short": "Kopun", "lat": 42.6407, "lng": 18.1102, "tags": ["Old Town · Jesuit square", "Confirmed trading 2026 (checked 22 Oct)"], "productTags": ["Heritage recipes", "Capon", "Šporki makaruli"], "why": "Kopun means capon, a castrated cockerel, and the restaurant took both its name and its point from the bird, which turns up in the city's Renaissance comedies of Marin Držić. The house cooks it slowly with orange and honey and serves it on Poljana Ruđera Boškovića, the square at the top of the Jesuit stairs. Falstaff's Croatia 2026 guide gives it 86 points and singles out the vegetarian dishes as well as the capon.", "address": "Poljana Ruđera Boškovića 7, 20000 Dubrovnik", "phone": "+385 20 323 969", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kopun+Dubrovnik", "price_range": "Mains about EUR 25–45 (German guide, undated, seen Oct 2026)", "reservation": "Book a few days ahead for the square terrace", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "Old Ragusan recipes on the Jesuit square, built around the capon the house is named after.", "verdict": "Worth the climb for dishes the rest of the Old Town does not cook, and the square is quieter than the streets below it. Order the capon and the šporki makaruli and skip the international side of the menu. Mid-priced for the walls. Winter opening is not confirmed in what we found, so call before building a November plan around it.", "signature": "Kopun: capon slow-cooked with orange and honey", "caveat": "Winter schedule not confirmed; most Old Town houses close for part of the winter", "dishes": [{"name": "Kopun", "note": "Capon with orange and honey, the house dish", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Šporki makaruli", "note": "The old Dubrovnik meat-sauce pasta, sweet-spiced", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Arancini", "note": "Candied bitter-orange peel, the local sweet", "kind": "sweet"}, {"name": "Vegetarian plates", "note": "Falstaff 2026 calls them excellent", "kind": "dish"}], "neighborhood": "Old Town · Jesuit square", "signal_chip": {"label": "Falstaff 86", "full": "Falstaff Restaurant Guide Croatia 2026: 86 points; capon is the highlight, vegetarian dishes also praised", "cosign": "Capon recipe from the Držić-era kitchen"}, "hours": "Unconfirmed: no 2026 season dates found. Open now likely but not confirmed; November–December not confirmed (Dubrovnik rules from 2024 oblige terrace users to trade at least one winter month)", "category": "houses", "hot_this_month": "Držić's capon with oranges and honey suits the first cool evenings; the house also lists šporki makaruli and arancini (checked 22 Oct 2026)."},
    {"id": "v11-lady-pi-pi", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 11, "badge": "OLD TOWN GRILL", "name": "Lady Pi-Pi", "short": "Lady Pi-Pi", "lat": 42.6424, "lng": 18.1098, "tags": ["Old Town · Peline", "Confirmed trading 2026 (checked 22 Oct)"], "productTags": ["Charcoal grill", "Vine terrace", "Walk-in only"], "why": "The grill sits near the top of the Old Town under the northern wall, an open charcoal fire in a corner and a terrace roofed in vines with the roofs falling away below. It takes no bookings, so the queue is part of the evening, and Time Out says to expect about a quarter of an hour. Tripadvisor listings show it reopened on 3 April 2026 and is now closed until Easter 2027.", "address": "Disputed: Antuninska 23 (Time Out) / Peline 25-b (corner.inc) / Peline 1 (old record), Old Town, 20000 Dubrovnik", "phone": "+385 20 321 154", "hours": "Seasonal: about April–mid October (Time Out: April–mid Oct; Tripadvisor: opened 3 Apr 2026, closed until Easter 2027). Closed now; reopens around Easter 2027 · Call ahead: Time Out gives 9:00–14:00 and 18:00–23:00 daily in season; Tripadvisor gives 9:00–21:00", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lady+Pi-Pi+Dubrovnik", "price_range": "EUR 25–40 pp (seen May 2026)", "reservation": "No reservations", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "A walk-in charcoal grill high in the Old Town under a vine roof, closed now until spring.", "verdict": "Simple grilled meat and fish at fair prices with one of the better views inside the walls, which is why the line forms. Good for crew, useless for anyone who will not queue. It is a summer house only: shut now, so it drops out of any October-to-Easter plan.", "signature": "The mixed grill platter", "caveat": "Closed until Easter 2027; walk-in only, queue in season", "dishes": [{"name": "Mixed grill platter", "note": "Meats off the charcoal, the plate most reviews name", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Grilled squid", "note": "Off the same fire", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Tuna steak", "note": "Reviewers' pick from the fish side", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Tiger prawns", "note": "Grilled, from the seafood list", "kind": "dish"}], "neighborhood": "Old Town · Peline", "signal_chip": {"label": "Walk-in grill", "full": "Charcoal grill on a vine terrace under the north wall; no reservations; April to mid October", "cosign": "Time Out Croatia"}, "category": "houses"},
    {"id": "v06-konoba-dubrava", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 6, "badge": "COUNTRY KONOBA", "name": "Konoba Dubrava", "short": "Konoba Dubrava", "lat": 42.6532, "lng": 18.1297, "tags": ["Srđ · Bosanka", "Not confirmed for 2026 — call ahead"], "productTags": ["Peka", "Lamb", "Pre-order"], "why": "Bosanka is a hamlet on Srđ, the ridge behind the city, and the konoba is a ten-minute drive up the hairpins. Its point is peka: lamb, veal or octopus sealed under an iron bell and buried in embers, which takes hours and has to be ordered by phone. Guides differ on the notice needed, from three to four hours. On the way down the terrace looks back over Lokrum and the islands.", "address": "Bosanka 5, 20207 Dubrovnik (10 min by car above Old Town)", "phone": "Call ahead: +385 95 420 4000 (French guide) / +385 20 411 030 (old record)", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Konoba+Dubrava+Dubrovnik", "price_range": "EUR 35–55 pp (seen May 2026)", "status": "unverified", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "A family konoba in Bosanka on Srđ, ten minutes up from the walls, cooking peka to order.", "verdict": "The easiest proper peka from a Dubrovnik berth, and worth the planning. Book the table and the bell together, a day ahead if you can. The rest of the menu is ordinary; the peka is why you go. We found no 2026-dated evidence of trading or winter hours, and the phone number differs between sources, so confirm before sending guests up the hill.", "signature": "Lamb peka, ordered by phone hours ahead", "caveat": "Peka needs 3–4 h notice; 2026 trading and winter hours not confirmed; phone numbers conflict", "dishes": [{"name": "Lamb peka", "note": "Under the bell in embers; order hours ahead", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Veal peka", "note": "Same method, veal and potatoes", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Octopus peka", "note": "The sea version of the bell", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Sour cherry strudel", "note": "Named by a Slovenian guide", "kind": "sweet"}], "reservation": "Call ahead; book table and peka together, 2–3 days ahead in season", "neighborhood": "Srđ · Bosanka", "signal_chip": {"label": "Peka to order", "full": "Lamb, veal and octopus peka under the bell; order 3–4 hours ahead", "cosign": "Family-run, Bosanka on Srđ"}, "hours": "Unconfirmed: no 2026 season or winter hours found. Open now not confirmed; November–December not confirmed", "category": "konoba", "hot_this_month": "Peka weather: order the lamb or octopus peka by 11:00 for lunch, before the early November sunset over Lokrum (checked 22 Oct 2026)."},
    {"id": "v09-konoba-konavoski-dvori", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 9, "badge": "RIVER KONOBA", "name": "Konoba Konavoski Dvori", "short": "Konoba Konavoski Dvori", "lat": 42.5532, "lng": 18.3447, "tags": ["Konavle · Ljuta", "Not confirmed for 2026 — call ahead"], "productTags": ["Watermill", "Frog brodet", "Traditional dress"], "why": "The restaurant occupies a restored watermill on the Ljuta, a cold spring river that drops through woodland in Konavle, the valley south of Cavtat towards Montenegro. The water runs past the terraces and through the old mill race. Staff wear Konavle costume, and the kitchen cooks what the valley cooks: trout from the river, frogs in brodet, lamb under the bell. It has fed families from Dubrovnik for generations.", "address": "Ljuta bb, 20210 Cavtat (Konavle, 35 min south of Dubrovnik)", "phone": "+385 20 791 039", "hours": "Unconfirmed: no 2026 season or winter hours found. Open now not confirmed; November–December not confirmed · Call ahead: In Your Pocket gives 11:00–23:00 (listing over a year old); another listing gives 12:00–24:00 daily", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Konoba+Konavoski+Dvori+Dubrovnik", "price_range": "EUR 45–65 pp (seen May 2026)", "reservation": "Book about a week ahead for weekend lunch", "status": "unverified", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "An old watermill on the Ljuta in Konavle, serving river trout, frog brodet and peka in the woods.", "verdict": "A lunch outing rather than a dinner, best combined with a drive through Konavle or a day at Cavtat. The costumes lean towards folklore, but the frog brodet and the trout are real local food you will not find in town. We found no 2026-dated evidence and no current MICHELIN listing, so confirm hours by phone, especially in winter.", "signature": "Žaba na brodet, frogs stewed the Konavle way", "caveat": "Winter hours and 2026 trading not confirmed; 35 minutes' drive from Dubrovnik", "dishes": [{"name": "Žaba na brodet", "note": "Frog stew, the valley dish the city does not cook", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "River trout", "note": "From the Ljuta beside the tables", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Lamb peka", "note": "Under the bell, order ahead", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Wild asparagus", "note": "In spring, from the old record", "kind": "dish"}], "neighborhood": "Konavle · Ljuta", "signal_chip": {"label": "River mill", "full": "Restored watermill on the Ljuta river in Konavle; staff in Konavle costume", "cosign": "Esculap group (per old record)"}, "category": "konoba", "hot_this_month": "A Sunday lunch after the last Čilipi folklore shows of the season; frog brodet and trout by the Ljuta, booked a week ahead for weekends (checked 22 Oct 2026)."},
    {"id": "v07-bota-are-mali-ston", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 7, "badge": "OYSTER HOUSE", "name": "Bota Šare Mali Ston", "short": "Bota Šare Mali Ston", "lat": 42.8497, "lng": 17.7042, "tags": ["Mali Ston", "Confirmed trading 2026 (checked 22 Oct)"], "productTags": ["PDO oysters", "At-source", "Sushi line"], "why": "Božidar Šare, known as Bota, opened this restaurant in Mali Ston with his wife Tanja a few decades ago, in a vaulted stone building by the harbour that was once a salt store. The family's farming and fishing ties to the bay explain the menu. From here the name spread to oyster and sushi bars in Dubrovnik, Split and Zagreb, which still take fish and shellfish from Mali Ston daily.", "address": "Mali Ston bb, 20230 Ston (15th-c. salt warehouse)", "phone": "+385 20 754 482", "hours": "Year-round per Time Out (Jan–Dec daily, listing with kuna prices, so dated). Open now and November–December likely; call to confirm · Call ahead: Time Out gives 11:00–24:00 daily; In Your Pocket 10:00–24:00; Tripadvisor 12:00–22:00", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bota+Šare+Mali+Ston+Dubrovnik", "price_range": "EUR 40–70 pp (seen May 2026)", "reservation": "Walk-in usually possible at lunch; book dinner in summer", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "The Šare family's oyster house in a vaulted Mali Ston salt store, the root of a Croatian chain.", "verdict": "The more polished of the two Mali Ston houses, and the safer pick for guests: vaulted room, sea view, oysters opened to order a few metres from the beds. The sushi side is a modern addition rather than a local tradition; stay with the oysters and shellfish. Listings say it trades all year, which makes it one of the few out-of-town tables to plan in November.", "signature": "A dozen Mali Ston oysters, raw with lemon", "caveat": "Year-round opening is from an older Time Out listing; call to confirm winter hours", "person": "Šare family (founder Božidar 'Bota' Šare)", "dishes": [{"name": "Mali Ston oysters", "note": "Ostrea edulis from the bay, raw", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Oyster tempura", "note": "Fried, the house's modern take", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Mussels na buzaru", "note": "In wine, garlic and parsley", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Prawn pasta", "note": "On Falstaff's list of the kitchen's dishes", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Pošip", "note": "The Dalmatian white the old record pairs with the oysters", "kind": "drink"}], "web": "https://www.bota-sare.hr/en/mali-ston", "neighborhood": "Mali Ston", "signal_chip": {"label": "At the source", "full": "Mali Ston oysters served a few metres from the beds; Gault&Millau Croatia 2026 reviews the family business; Falstaff 2025: 85 points", "cosign": "Šare family, founders of the Bota oyster bars"}, "category": "oysters", "hot_this_month": "Inside the oyster season again: the season runs about September to April (peak is March); lunch walk-in is possible, but phone ahead in winter (checked 22 Oct 2026).", "charter": {"price": "EUR 40–70 pp (seen May 2026)", "book": "Walk-in usually possible at lunch; book dinner in summer", "warn": "Year-round opening is from an older Time Out listing; call to confirm winter hours", "fit": "The Šare family's oyster house in a vaulted Mali Ston salt store, the root of a Croatian chain."}},
    {"id": "v08-vila-koruna", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 8, "badge": "OYSTER HOUSE 1973", "name": "Vila Koruna", "short": "Vila Koruna", "lat": 42.8496, "lng": 17.7038, "tags": ["Mali Ston", "Not confirmed for 2026 — call ahead"], "productTags": ["Oyster house since 1973", "Rustic", "Rooms above"], "why": "Vila Koruna bills itself as the oldest eating house in the area and has been serving Mali Ston oysters since 1973. Its shellfish and fish wait in stone tanks on the terrace, glass-fronted and filled with seawater drawn from 48 metres down. A Valamar writer counted oysters done eleven ways, from raw with wild orange to fried and in soup. There are six guest rooms above the dining room.", "address": "Mali Ston bb, 20230 Ston", "phone": "+385 20 754 999", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Vila+Koruna+Dubrovnik", "price_range": "EUR 35–55 pp (seen May 2026)", "reservation": "Walk-in usually fine outside high summer (old record); call ahead off-season", "status": "unverified", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "The old family oyster house on Mali Ston bay, with seawater tanks on the terrace and rooms upstairs.", "verdict": "The plainer, older-feeling of the two Mali Ston houses, good for oysters, mussels and a long lunch by the water without ceremony. Fine for a Pelješac overnight. We found no 2026-dated evidence that it is trading and no winter hours, so this one needs a phone call before it goes on any guest list.", "signature": "Oysters raw from the terrace tanks, then mussels na buzaru", "caveat": "2026 trading and winter hours not confirmed; call first", "dishes": [{"name": "Oysters raw", "note": "With lemon or wild orange, from the terrace tanks", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Baked or fried oysters", "note": "Two of the eleven ways the house serves them", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Mussels na buzaru", "note": "Wine and garlic, the bay's other shellfish", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Grilled scampi", "note": "From the old record", "kind": "dish"}], "neighborhood": "Mali Ston", "signal_chip": {"label": "Since 1973", "full": "Family oyster house on Mali Ston bay since 1973; seawater tanks on the terrace; six rooms", "cosign": "In Your Pocket Dubrovnik"}, "hours": "Unconfirmed: no 2026 season or winter hours found. Open now not confirmed; November–December not confirmed", "category": "oysters", "hot_this_month": "Its off-season shape: lunch, oysters au naturel and mussels na buzaru, walk-in fine now the summer is over; pair it with a walk over the Ston walls (checked 22 Oct 2026)."},
    {"id": "v-taj-mahal", "cat": "shop", "tier": "plenty", "priority": 1, "name": "Taj Mahal (Bosnian grill)", "short": "Taj Mahal", "lat": null, "lng": null, "tags": ["Old Town · Gučetića", "Confirmed trading 2026 (checked 22 Oct)"], "productTags": ["Bosnian grill"], "address": "Nikole Gučetića 2, 20000 Dubrovnik", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Taj+Mahal+Nikole+Gucetica+Dubrovnik+Croatia", "why": "The name has nothing to do with India: this is the Old Town's Bosnian house, on Nikole Gučetića just off the Stradun. MICHELIN lists it as a Bib Gourmand and says the meat on the grill comes from the family's own butcher, and the plum baklava is made by the owner's mother. There is a second, roomier branch in Hotel Lero, a few kilometres up toward Gruž, for nights the alley is full.", "verdict": "Good-value Balkan cooking with a guide's backing, in a part of town where value is rare. Expect meat, kajmak and bread in quantity, not seafood. Book: the small room fills, and MICHELIN itself advises reservations. A sound last-minute table for crew or guests who are tired of grilled fish.", "signature": "The Taj Mahal special: veal with mushrooms in a crisp pastry shell.", "caveat": "Small and popular, book ahead; winter hours not confirmed, call +385 20 323 221.", "person": "", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "Bosnian family kitchen inside the walls, MICHELIN Bib Gourmand, grilled meat from its own butcher.", "dishes": [{"name": "Taj Mahal special", "note": "Veal with mushrooms baked in a crisp shell, Time Out's pick", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Peppers stuffed with kajmak", "note": "Fried peppers filled with Bosnian cream cheese", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Ćevapi in lepinja", "note": "Grilled minced-meat fingers in flatbread with onion and ajvar", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Plum baklava", "note": "Made by the owner's mother, per MICHELIN", "kind": "sweet"}], "hours": "Not confirmed for winter; Time Out (undated) lists daily hours with no seasonal break · Call ahead: Time Out (undated) daily 09:00–01:00; no other source gives hours", "phone": "+385 20 323 221", "price_range": "MICHELIN €€ (seen Oct 2026)", "reservation": "Recommended (MICHELIN)", "neighborhood": "Old Town · Gučetića", "badge": "BIB GOURMAND", "signal_chip": {"label": "Bib Gourmand", "full": "MICHELIN Bib Gourmand, Dubrovnik, listed in the Croatia selection; a 2026 Croatia list notes two consecutive Bibs", "cosign": "Time Out 4/5"}, "category": "locals", "charter": {"price": "MICHELIN €€ (seen Oct 2026)", "book": "Recommended (MICHELIN)", "warn": "Small and popular, book ahead; winter hours not confirmed, call +385 20 323 221.", "fit": "Bosnian family kitchen inside the walls, MICHELIN Bib Gourmand, grilled meat from its own butcher."}},
    {"id": "v13-pizzeria-tabasco", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 13, "badge": "PIZZERIA", "name": "Pizzeria Tabasco", "short": "Pizzeria Tabasco", "lat": 42.6428, "lng": 18.1158, "tags": ["Ploče · Hvarska", "Not confirmed for 2026 — call ahead"], "productTags": ["Decade-deep", "Walls view", "Late dinner"], "why": "Tabasco sits on Hvarska, the lane that climbs from outside the eastern walls toward the cable-car station, which is why locals rather than day-trippers fill it. Lonely Planet notes the pizzas come out of a wood oven and that it does takeaway and delivery when the terrace is full; In Your Pocket says the beer is among the cheapest near the Old Town. Listings give it the same hours all year, a little shorter in winter.", "address": "Hvarska 48a, 20000 Dubrovnik (also listed as Hvarska 48)", "phone": "+385 20 429 595", "hours": "Year-round per listings (undated): summer May–October and winter hours both given; 2026 not confirmed · Call ahead: Absolute Croatia and Time Out: May–Oct daily 09:30–24:00, winter daily 09:30–23:00; Trip.com: 10:00–23:00", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pizzeria+Tabasco+Dubrovnik", "price_range": "Below Old Town prices per In Your Pocket; no 2026 menu prices found (seen Oct 2026)", "reservation": "Walk-in; takeaway and delivery offered", "status": "unverified", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "Wood-fired pizzeria between the Ploče gate and the cable car, cheap beer and very large panzerotti.", "verdict": "A plain, honest pizzeria, not a destination: Time Out gives it three stars out of five and calls it standard, and that is fair. Its value is being open late, every day, a short walk from the walls, at prices well under the Stradun. Send crew here after service, or guests who want pizza without a scene.", "signature": "A wood-fired pizza, or the oversized panzerotto.", "caveat": "No 2026-dated evidence found; hours and phone vary across listings, call ahead.", "dishes": [{"name": "Wood-fired pizza", "note": "Light dough with fresh toppings, the reason people come", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Panzerotti", "note": "Fried folded pizza; Time Out calls them enormous", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Draught beer", "note": "Among the cheapest pours near the Old Town", "kind": "drink"}], "neighborhood": "Ploče · Hvarska", "signal_chip": {"label": "Locals' pizza", "full": "In Your Pocket: local and tourist opinion rates it the best pizza in Dubrovnik; Time Out 3/5", "cosign": "Lonely Planet: a locals' favourite, wood-fired"}, "category": "locals"},
    {"id": "v14-d-vino-wine-bar", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 14, "badge": "WINE BAR", "name": "D'vino Wine Bar", "short": "D'vino Wine Bar", "lat": 42.6416, "lng": 18.1089, "productTags": ["Croatian wines only", "60+ by glass", "Flights"], "why": "D'vino sits on Palmotićeva, one of the stepped lanes north of the Stradun, and was built around one idea: let a visitor taste the country without buying bottles. The bar's own site claims more than 60 wines by the glass, the largest such list in Dubrovnik, and the flights of Croatian whites and reds come with English notes. Total Croatia News names Sasha Lušić as the owner who runs the room.", "address": "Palmotićeva 4a, 20000 Dubrovnik", "phone": "+385 20 321 130", "hours": "Seasonal per Total Croatia News (undated): roughly April to late October; 2026 closing date not found, possibly closing now · Call ahead: Time Out (undated) daily 10:00–24:00; Cityzeum (2026 update) daily 12:00–24:00", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=D%27vino+Wine+Bar+Dubrovnik", "price_range": "EUR 25–55 pp (flights ~EUR 15–25) (seen May 2026)", "reservation": "Walk-in for the bar", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "Old Town wine bar off the Stradun pouring Croatian bottles by the glass and in tasting flights.", "verdict": "The most efficient way to learn Pelješac, Korčula and Konavle wine in one sitting before the dinners and cellar visits. It is a bar, small plates at most, and tourist-facing by design, so it runs on the season. Check it is still open before building a late-October aperitivo around it.", "signature": "A flight of Croatian reds built around Plavac Mali.", "caveat": "Seasonal per Total Croatia News (about April–late October); may already be closed for winter, call first.", "person": "Sasha Lušić (owner, per Total Croatia News, undated)", "dishes": [{"name": "Croatian red flight", "note": "Several Plavac Mali-led pours side by side", "kind": "drink"}, {"name": "Croatian white flight", "note": "Pošip, Grk and other Dalmatian whites in one run", "kind": "drink"}, {"name": "Wine by the glass", "note": "60+ open bottles per the bar's own site", "kind": "drink"}], "web": "https://dvino.net/", "neighborhood": "Old Town · Palmotićeva", "signal_chip": {"label": "60+ by glass", "full": "Own site: over 60 wines by the glass, the largest selection in Dubrovnik (self-description); Time Out says 100+ wines stocked", "cosign": "Total Croatia News wine-bar feature"}, "category": "glass", "hot_this_month": "A Plavac Mali flight from Pelješac in the week of Martinje, 11 November, when the country toasts the young wine (checked 22 Oct 2026)."},
    {"id": "v17-grgi-vina-cellar-door", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 17, "badge": "WINERY", "name": "Grgić Vina (cellar door)", "short": "Grgić Vina (cellar door)", "lat": 42.9067, "lng": 17.4847, "tags": ["Pelješac · Trstenik", "Confirmed trading 2026 (checked 22 Oct)"], "productTags": ["Mike Grgich", "Plavac Mali", "Pošip"], "why": "Miljenko Grgich left Croatia, made the Chardonnay that won the 1976 Paris tasting, and came back in 1996 to build a winery on the headland above Trstenik. It still makes just two wines, and the tasting covers both. Falstaff tasted them in April 2026 and gave the 2022 Plavac Mali and the 2024 Pošip 93 points each, and lists the house in its 2026 guide.", "address": "Trstenik 78, 20245 Trstenik (Pelješac)", "phone": "+385 20 748 090", "hours": "Time Out (undated): April–November daily 09:00–17:00; Lonely Planet: call ahead in winter. Likely open now and into November; December not confirmed · Time Out (undated): April–November daily 09:00–17:00; Frommer's: daily 09:00–17:00 but unreliable outside July–August", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Grgić+Vina+(cellar+door)+Dubrovnik", "price_range": "Tasting fee covers both wines; no 2026 price found (seen Oct 2026)", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "Mike Grgich's Pelješac homecoming above Trstenik: two wines, Plavac Mali and Pošip, tasted side by side.", "verdict": "A short, focused visit rather than a long estate tour: two glasses, a view over the Trstenik bay and a story every wine-minded guest will know. Pair it with lunch on Pelješac. Outside July and August the family-run schedule can slip, and nobody may be free to guide you; ring first.", "signature": "The Plavac Mali next to the Pošip.", "caveat": "Call ahead outside peak season; Time Out gives April–November only.", "dishes": [{"name": "Grgić Plavac Mali", "note": "The red; Falstaff 93 for the 2022 (April 2026)", "kind": "drink"}, {"name": "Grgić Pošip", "note": "The white; Falstaff 93 for the 2024 (April 2026)", "kind": "drink"}], "reservation": "Call or email ahead, especially off-season", "neighborhood": "Pelješac · Trstenik", "signal_chip": {"label": "Falstaff 93", "full": "Falstaff (Peter Moser, 17 Apr 2026): Plavac Mali 2022 93 pts, Pošip 2024 93 pts; listed in Falstaff 2026", "cosign": "Founded 1996 by Mike Grgich"}, "category": "glass", "hot_this_month": "After the harvest, by appointment only: email a week ahead for a tasting of the Plavac Mali and Pošip around Martinje (checked 22 Oct 2026)."},
    {"id": "v18-milo-stagnum", "cat": "shop", "tier": "several", "priority": 18, "badge": "WINERY", "name": "Miloš Stagnum", "short": "Miloš Stagnum", "lat": 42.9105, "lng": 17.491, "tags": ["Pelješac · Ponikve", "Confirmed trading 2026 (checked 22 Oct)"], "productTags": ["Cult wine", "Organic", "Old Slavonian oak"], "why": "Above Ston at Ponikve, the Miloš family farms Plavac Mali organically and ages its top red, Stagnum, in large old Slavonian oak. Hugh Johnson called it the first Croatian cult wine. Falstaff's Peter Moser tasted the 2016 in April 2026, scored it 94 and called it a traditional icon of the peninsula. The tasting room is built into the rock of the hillside.", "address": "Ponikve 15, 20230 Ston (Pelješac)", "phone": "+385 20 742 393", "hours": "Not confirmed for 2026; Time Out (undated) lists daily hours with no season; book by phone · Call ahead: Time Out (undated) daily 08:00–21:00; old record says by appointment", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Miloš+Stagnum+Dubrovnik", "price_range": "Tasting EUR 35–60 pp (seen May 2026)", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "The Miloš family's organic Plavac Mali house at Ponikve, maker of Stagnum, tasted in a rock-cut room.", "verdict": "The serious red stop on Pelješac, for guests who want to taste aged Plavac Mali rather than the fresh style. Tastings are quiet and unhurried. Fit it on the way back from Ston oysters; book in advance, since this is a family house, not a visitor centre.", "signature": "An older vintage of Stagnum.", "caveat": "Book ahead; listed hours are undated and 2026 tasting prices were not found.", "dishes": [{"name": "Stagnum", "note": "The long-aged Plavac Mali; 2016 scored 94 by Falstaff in April 2026", "kind": "drink"}, {"name": "Plavac Mali", "note": "The younger estate red", "kind": "drink"}, {"name": "Rosé", "note": "The lighter Plavac wine Time Out mentions", "kind": "drink"}], "web": "https://milos.hr/", "reservation": "By appointment", "neighborhood": "Pelješac · Ponikve", "signal_chip": {"label": "Falstaff 94", "full": "Falstaff (Peter Moser, 17 Apr 2026): Miloš Stagnum 2016, 94 pts", "cosign": "Hugh Johnson: Croatia's first cult wine"}, "category": "glass"},
    {"id": "v16-gru-market-tr-nica-gru", "cat": "market", "tier": "several", "priority": 16, "badge": "MARKET", "name": "Gruž Market (Tržnica Gruž)", "short": "Gruž Market (Tržnica Gru", "lat": 42.6612, "lng": 18.089, "tags": ["Gruž", "Not confirmed for 2026 — call ahead"], "productTags": ["Provisioning", "Fish hall", "Cash"], "why": "On the Gruž waterfront, opposite the ferry and cruise berths, the city's working market sells produce from the Konavle and Rijeka Dubrovačka growers outdoors and fish under cover. Time Out says the fish comes in from the Elafiti islands and to arrive by seven for the best of it. Absolute Croatia says Friday and Saturday are the busiest days, and that prices soften toward closing.", "address": "Obala Stjepana Radića, 20000 Dubrovnik", "hours": "Year-round (Time Out gives summer and winter hours); 2026 not specifically confirmed · Call ahead: Time Out (undated) summer 06:00–20:00, winter 06:00–18:00, Sun 06:00–11:00; Absolute Croatia 06:30–13:00, to about 15:00 in summer", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Gruž+Market+(Tržnica+Gruž)+Dubrovnik", "status": "unverified", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "Gruž harbour's open market and fish hall, where boats from the Elafiti land the morning catch.", "verdict": "The provisioning stop for any boat lying in Gruž: real fish, real vegetables, cash in hand. Go early, because the fish hall thins out fast. Do not expect a food hall; it is a market for buying, not for eating.", "signature": "The morning's fish from the Elafiti boats.", "caveat": "Cash only on most stalls; come before 07:00 for fish; hours conflict across listings.", "dishes": [{"name": "Fish of the morning", "note": "Landed from the Elafiti; best before 07:00", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Seasonal produce", "note": "Fruit, vegetables and herbs from local growers on the open stalls", "kind": "dish"}], "reservation": "None", "neighborhood": "Gruž", "signal_chip": {"label": "Fish at 07:00", "full": "Time Out: arrive by 07:00 for the best fish from the Elafiti islands", "cosign": "Absolute Croatia: busiest Fri–Sat"}, "category": "street", "hot_this_month": "Provision early: the boats land about 06:30 and the fish is gone by 10:00; plan around the holidays of 1 and 18 November (checked 22 Oct 2026)."},
    {"id": "v12-buffet-kola", "cat": "berth", "tier": "berth_top", "priority": 3, "badge": "SANDWICH BAR", "name": "Buffet Škola", "short": "Buffet Škola", "lat": 42.6416, "lng": 18.1088, "tags": ["Old Town · Antuninska", "Confirmed trading 2026 (checked 22 Oct)"], "productTags": ["50+ years", "Pršut", "Cash"], "why": "On Antuninska, a stepped lane off the Stradun, Škola does one thing: a sandwich on bread baked in the house, filled with pršut from Drniš in the Dalmatian hinterland and cheese from Konavle south of the city. It made both the Gault&Millau Croatia 2026 and Falstaff 2026 guides, the latter at 82 points, which is rare for a place with three tables. There is a special menu with vegetarian, vegan and gluten-free choices.", "address": "Antuninska 1, 20000 Dubrovnik", "phone": "Call ahead: +385 20 321 096 or +385 91 626 2640 (both listed)", "hours": "Year-round per listings (undated); winter hours not confirmed · Call ahead: In Your Pocket (old) 09:00–24:00, Sun 09:00–21:00; no 2026 hours found", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Buffet+Škola+Dubrovnik", "price_range": "EUR 8–15 pp (seen May 2026)", "reservation": "Walk-in; eat in or take away", "status": "confirmed", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "A tiny Old Town sandwich counter: warm house bread, Drniš pršut and Konavle cheese, in Gault&Millau 2026.", "verdict": "The best cheap lunch inside the walls and the quickest: order, eat standing or take it to the harbour. It is not a restaurant and does not pretend to be. Good for crew between jobs and for guests who want one honest local bite between the walls walk and the boat.", "signature": "The pršut and Konavle cheese sandwich on warm house bread.", "caveat": "Three tables only; hours and phone vary across listings.", "dishes": [{"name": "Pršut and cheese sandwich", "note": "Drniš pršut and Konavle cheese on warm house bread", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "House bread", "note": "Baked on site, the base of everything", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Glass of domestic red", "note": "From the old record; the obvious pairing", "kind": "drink"}], "neighborhood": "Old Town · Antuninska", "signal_chip": {"label": "G&M + Falstaff", "full": "Listed in Gault&Millau Croatia 2026 and Falstaff 2026 street food (82 pts)", "cosign": "Total Croatia News budget pick"}, "category": "street"},
    {"id": "v-barba", "cat": "shop", "tier": "plenty", "priority": 1, "name": "Barba", "short": "Barba", "lat": null, "lng": null, "tags": ["Old Town · Boškovićeva", "Not confirmed for 2026 — call ahead"], "productTags": ["Seafood street food"], "address": "Boškovićeva 5, 20000 Dubrovnik", "maps": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Barba+Boskoviceva+5+Dubrovnik+Croatia", "why": "Barba, Dalmatian for uncle, takes local fish and puts it in a bun: octopus burger, shrimp and tuna burgers, anchovy sandwiches, fried calamari, shrimp tacos, and an octopus sandwich with mascarpone. It is a counter with a few seats on Boškovićeva, a narrow lane a minute from the Stradun. A Wanderlog list updated in November 2025 still counted it among the city's street-food stops.", "verdict": "Worth one visit for the octopus burger, which most reviewers praise; past that the record is mixed, with complaints of heavy batter and a poor shrimp burger. Fast, cheap by Old Town standards, crowded at peak. Go off-hours and keep it to the octopus.", "signature": "The octopus burger.", "caveat": "No 2026-dated evidence; hours conflict and winter opening unknown; call +385 91 205 3488.", "person": "", "status": "unverified", "statusChecked": "2026-10-22", "hook": "Old Town seafood counter off the Stradun turning the day's catch into octopus burgers and anchovy sandwiches.", "dishes": [{"name": "Octopus burger", "note": "The plate everyone orders; reviewers find it tender", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Anchovy sandwich", "note": "Local salted or marinated anchovies in bread", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Fried calamari", "note": "Paper cone, eat on the street", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Octopus sandwich with mascarpone", "note": "The combination Time Out singles out", "kind": "dish"}, {"name": "Shrimp tacos", "note": "Named in several write-ups", "kind": "dish"}], "hours": "Not confirmed; no winter dates found · Call ahead: one guide 11:00–20:00; In Your Pocket 11:00–24:00; Time Out 11:00–23:00", "phone": "+385 91 205 3488", "price_range": "Octopus burger about EUR 8 (blogger, undated); shrimp burger EUR 14 (2024 review) (seen Oct 2026)", "reservation": "Walk-in only", "neighborhood": "Old Town · Boškovićeva", "badge": "SEAFOOD STREET", "signal_chip": {"label": "Octopus burger", "full": "Time Out 4/5; Wanderlog list (Nov 2025) of top Dubrovnik street food", "cosign": "Afar and In Your Pocket listings"}, "category": "street"}
